## CORE instruction length limits (ChatGPT/Gemini/Copilot)

### Hard rule (absolute)
- When producing CORE instructions for ChatGPT Project/Custom GPT, Gemini GEMS, or Copilot Agent, the CORE instruction text MUST be <= 8000 characters total.
- The assistant MUST NOT output a CORE file that exceeds 8000 characters.
- If a draft would exceed 8000, shorten by moving execution detail into COMPANION and re-check length.

### Target rule (recommended)
- Target CORE <= 6000 characters.
- If CORE would exceed 6000 characters, warn the user and ask whether to override the target.
- If the user approves, CORE may exceed 6000 but must still remain <= 8000.

### Counting guidance (what to count)
- Count ALL characters in the CORE file content, including header lines, whitespace, and punctuation.
- Provide a character-count estimate in chat text OUTSIDE the file block (never inside the CORE file content).

### Default strategy to stay under limits
- CORE contains: governance, prohibitions, routing, schemas/format locks, and intake gating rules.
- COMPANION contains: execution logic details, step-by-step procedures, long examples, and the change log for CORE and COMPANION.
